  "observations": [
    "A uses saved Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F12, B uses saved Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F11 in separate owned configs. Mappings are prepared fixtures, not acceptance of editor gestures. Both are ordinary GUI337/Core265/library282/recording322 with generated media.",
    "OS keyboard delivery targets a separate native owned Qt window. A starts from paused zero, advances, and pauses at progress0.2844143573678159. Foreground settled readback reports17seconds. Background accessibility snapshots can remain stale even when the rendered clock and Play/Pause state change.",
    "B starts E02 from zero and pauses at progress0.2037564113245905, about12seconds. A remains paused at the exact previous progress after both B chords. A closes normally; B still starts through its F11 global chord and advances. B is then paused at progress0.5691123294062755 before settings.",
    "The traditional Advanced Preferences dialog opens from General Advanced Options. Mouse accessibility activation of Simple fails with element unavailable; the native dialog is on the other monitor and not separately returned by the window list. Keyboard navigation selects Simple, follows the category buttons to Hotkeys, and renders the full table including the saved Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F11 value. Escape cancels without saving. The paused player retains progress0.5691123294062755.",
    "Both ordinary applications exit0, load602modules, log zero checked error diagnostics and pass all original source/runtime/fixture/producer/cache guards. The separate focus helper closes normally before its timeout with unchanged helper and QML. No forced cleanup is used."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This qualifies two distinct Play/Pause combinations, held-player isolation and survival after the first instance exits. It does not establish all shortcut actions, same-chord conflict feedback, live remapping, both closing orders or broad OS key ownership.",
    "B explicitly guards the Windows global-key DLL and win32.c source in its frozen inventory. A original runtime guard did not enumerate that DLL; no broader binary guard is retroactively claimed for A.",
    "An initial occluded target capture shows VLC pixels; activating the target produces its actual dark window. Several immediate snapshots have stale accessibility text; the later settled screenshots/readbacks are the relevant state evidence.",
    "All profiles and media are owned test fixtures. Raw logs, configs, databases, media and binaries stay ignored locally. No dependency, privacy or security changes were made. Full design, accessibility, Windows DPI and final-package gates remain open."
  ],
